+### `tiled-groups`
+
+<sup>Since: next release</sup> (experimental)
+
+Automatically stitches tiled monitors (panels connected over two independent links on the same GPU, e.g. the LG UltraFine 5K over two DisplayPort SST links) into single logical outputs, using the kernel-reported `TILE` connector topology.
+
+A pair is only stitched when both tiles advertise a horizontal 2x1 single-monitor topology with the same EDID identity, expose the same primary-plane pixel formats, and share a mode with byte-identical timings; otherwise the connectors stay separate outputs and the reason is logged with a `tiled-groups:` prefix.
+
+Explicit [`tiled-group`](./Configuration:-Outputs.md#tiled-group) output config does not require this flag and is authoritative over auto-detection.
+
+```kdl
+debug {
+    tiled-groups
+}
+```
+
 ### Key Bindings
 
 These are not debug options, but rather key bindings.
